# TRACKER — live session auto-record ledger (narrative surface)

`bin/track --once` runs one STATELESS reconciliation tick against `.pm/index.json` + a fresh
`herdr api snapshot`. For every `ACKED` dispatch whose recorded tab shows `done`, it evaluates a
strict git-corroboration predicate: fully corroborated tabs are auto-recorded as `RETURNED`
(intake only — never auto-verified); everything else is surfaced below with the reason it was
NOT auto-recorded, so the operator can act. Working/blocked tabs are not evaluated and do not
appear here.

The same tick also runs the auto-close pass (config-gated on `automation.auto_close`, default
OFF): an issue closes only when it passes the human-state gates (VERIFIED dispatch, no open
questions, clean dispatch graph) AND strict git topology corroborates the result on the
configured mainline. For repos configured `merge_mode: "squash"` (squash/rebase workflows,
where the branch tip never lands on mainline verbatim), strict is still tried first; on a
strict-topology miss the pass consults a human-attested `merged` marker (`record merged`).
Be clear about what that means: a marker close is **human attestation sanity-checked by
git**, not git corroboration that the work landed — git verifies only that the attested
merge commit is real and on mainline (a squash destroys the ancestry that would prove more),
so setting `merge_mode: "squash"` is an explicit statement that you accept human-attested
auto-closes for that repo. Rows below always say which path closed an issue
(`auto-closed-strict` vs `auto-closed-marker`, with an explicit
`auto-closed-marker-branch-deleted` variant that additionally requires the per-repo
`allow_marker_branch_deleted: true` opt-in when the worker branch was already cleaned up),
and every marker close leaves a durable `auto-close:*` audit note on the event log before
the close itself. Everything else is surfaced with a reason, never closed.

> Human narrative only. Authoritative state is the event log; `bin/track` renders the block
> below fresh on every `--once` tick (pure function of index/snapshot/git — unchanged state
> re-renders byte-identical).

